  "lean": {
    "statement": "\n    {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]\n    [CompleteSpace E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E]\n    [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]\n    (f : E → ℝ) (hf : ContDiff ℝ 2 f) (hs : HasCompactSupport f) :\n    let γ : Measure E := ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E\n    Integrable (fun x => (f x)^2) γ ∧\n    Integrable (fun x => (f x)^2 * Real.log ((f x)^2)) γ ∧\n    Integrable (fun x => ‖gradient f x‖^2) γ ∧\n    (∫ x, (f x)^2 * Real.log ((f x)^2) ∂γ) -\n      (∫ x, (f x)^2 ∂γ) * Real.log (∫ x, (f x)^2 ∂γ) ≤\n      2 * ∫ x, ‖gradient f x‖^2 ∂γ",
    "statement_sha256": "2a017a8833807d327f3627bbe55465f4b0490fcfde7418e8158f0b87a1f1b02f",
    "compiled": true,
    "approved_definition_context": [
      "E is any finite-dimensional complete real inner-product space with its compatible norm and Borel measurable structure, including rank zero.",
      "f is a signed real function, globally twice continuously Frechet differentiable and compactly supported. These are the only analytic premises.",
      "ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E is the literal canonical standard Gaussian measure: map of independent centered variance-one real Gaussian coordinates under the canonical orthonormal basis sum. No supplied measure/covariance certificate is a premise.",
      "gradient is the literal global Mathlib Riesz representative of the real Frechet derivative on this Hilbert space. Its norm is the Hilbert norm; no default-Pi sup operator norm or surrogate coordinate energy is substituted.",
      "All displayed integrals are real Bochner integrals; the three Integrable conclusions provide genuine L1 domains under the actual law. Real.log is totalized at0.",
      "The entropy is homogeneous square entropy, with no unit-mass, positivity, integrability, law-map, gradient-Parseval or desired-inequality certificate premise. Signed f and zero mass are included."
    ]
  },
